# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operations into boxes {#group-operations-into-boxes}"
msgstr "I-group ang mga operasyon sa mga box {#group-operations-into-boxes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The argument `enable_gates` can be set to `True` or `False` to specify whether the two-qubit gates should be grouped into boxes. Similarly, `enable_measures` specifies whether or not measurements should be grouped. The following snippet shows an example where both gates and measurements are grouped.\n"
msgstr "Ang argument na `enable_gates` ay maaaring itakda sa `True` o `False` para tukuyin kung dapat bang i-group sa mga box ang mga two-qubit gate. Gayundin, tinutukoy ng `enable_measures` kung dapat bang i-group ang mga measurement o hindi. Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na snippet ang isang halimbawa kung saan parehong naka-group ang mga gate at measurement.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/b323dde8a5412e42359aef1831af92ed3702d2251547c663208dc084a2995276.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/b323dde8a5412e42359aef1831af92ed3702d2251547c663208dc084a2995276.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/b323dde8a5412e42359aef1831af92ed3702d2251547c663208dc084a2995276.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/b323dde8a5412e42359aef1831af92ed3702d2251547c663208dc084a2995276.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As can be seen in the figure, the pass manager creates boxes of two types: those that contain a single layer of two-qubit gates, and those that contain a single layer of measurements. This separation reflects standard practices in noise learning and mitigation protocols, which usually target layers of homogeneous operations. The two-qubit gates and measurements are placed in the leftmost box that can accommodate them, and every single-qubit gates is placed in the same box as the two-qubit gate or measurement they preceed.\n"
msgstr "Gaya ng makikita sa figure, gumagawa ang pass manager ng mga box na may dalawang uri: ang mga naglalaman ng iisang layer ng mga two-qubit gate, at ang mga naglalaman ng iisang layer ng mga measurement. Sinasalamin ng paghihiwalay na ito ang mga karaniwang gawi sa mga protocol ng noise learning at mitigation, na karaniwang tumatarget sa mga layer ng homogeneous na operasyon. Ang mga two-qubit gate at measurement ay inilalagay sa pinakakaliwang box na kayang tumanggap sa kanila, at bawat single-qubit gate ay inilalagay sa parehong box ng two-qubit gate o measurement na sinusundan nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code shows an example where `enable_gates` is set to `False`. As can be seen, the two-qubit gates are not grouped into boxes, nor are the single-qubit gates that preceed them.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na code ang isang halimbawa kung saan ang `enable_gates` ay nakatakda sa `False`. Gaya ng makikita, hindi naka-group sa mga box ang mga two-qubit gate, ni ang mga single-qubit gate na nauuna sa mga ito.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/3fc8e660b0c7eff1f5aa2e571d064f91b3eb2738c5990727e026a8ffe1101a1c.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/3fc8e660b0c7eff1f5aa2e571d064f91b3eb2738c5990727e026a8ffe1101a1c.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/3fc8e660b0c7eff1f5aa2e571d064f91b3eb2738c5990727e026a8ffe1101a1c.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/3fc8e660b0c7eff1f5aa2e571d064f91b3eb2738c5990727e026a8ffe1101a1c.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose how to annotate the boxes {#choose-how-to-annotate-the-boxes}"
msgstr "Piliin kung paano i-annotate ang mga box {#choose-how-to-annotate-the-boxes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All the two-qubit gates and measurement boxes in the returned circuit own left-dressed annotations. In particular, all the boxes that contain two-qubit gates are annotated with a `Twirl`. For measurement boxes, users can choose between `Twirl`, `BasisTranform` (with `mode` set to `\"measure\"`), or both. The following code generates a circuit where all the boxes are twirled, and the measurement boxes are additionally annotated with `BasisTranform`.\n"
msgstr "Lahat ng two-qubit gate at measurement box sa ibinalik na circuit ay may hawak na mga left-dressed na annotation. Sa partikular, lahat ng box na naglalaman ng mga two-qubit gate ay may annotation na `Twirl`. Para sa mga measurement box, maaaring pumili ang mga user sa pagitan ng `Twirl`, `BasisTranform` (na ang `mode` ay nakatakda sa `\"measure\"`), o pareho. Bumubuo ang sumusunod na code ng circuit kung saan lahat ng box ay naka-twirl, at ang mga measurement box ay dagdag na may annotation na `BasisTranform`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the circuit for noise injection {#prepare-the-circuit-for-noise-injection}"
msgstr "Ihanda ang circuit para sa noise injection {#prepare-the-circuit-for-noise-injection}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `inject_noise_targets` lets you specify which boxes should receive an `InjectNoise` annotation. For example, the following code generates a circuit where the two-qubit gates boxes own an `InjectNoise` annotation but the measurement boxes don’t.\n"
msgstr "Pinapayagan ka ng `inject_noise_targets` na tukuyin kung aling mga box ang dapat makatanggap ng annotation na `InjectNoise`. Halimbawa, bumubuo ang sumusunod na code ng circuit kung saan ang mga box ng two-qubit gate ay may hawak na annotation na `InjectNoise` pero ang mga measurement box ay wala.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a circuit contains two or more boxes that are equivalent up to single-qubit gates, all of them are annotated with an `InjectNoise` annotation with the same `ref`. Thus, the number of unique `ref`s in the returned circuit is equal to the number of unique boxes.\n"
msgstr "Kung ang isang circuit ay naglalaman ng dalawa o higit pang box na magkatumbas hanggang sa mga single-qubit gate, lahat ng mga ito ay ina-annotate ng annotation na `InjectNoise` na may parehong `ref`. Kaya, ang bilang ng mga natatanging `ref` sa ibinalik na circuit ay katumbas ng bilang ng mga natatanging box.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The value for `inject_noise_strategy` impacts the `InjectNoise` annotations. The following values are possible:\n"
msgstr "Ang value ng `inject_noise_strategy` ay may epekto sa mga annotation na `InjectNoise`. Posible ang mga sumusunod na value:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`modifier_ref=''`: Recommended when you don’t have to modify the noise maps before sampling from them.\n"
msgstr "`modifier_ref=''`: Inirerekomenda kapag hindi mo kailangang baguhin ang mga noise map bago mag-sample mula sa mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`modifier_ref=ref`: Recommended when all the noise maps need to be scaled uniformly by the same factor.\n"
msgstr "`modifier_ref=ref`: Inirerekomenda kapag kailangang i-scale nang pantay ang lahat ng noise map sa parehong factor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A unique value of `modifier_ref`: Recommended when every noise map needs to be scaled by a different factor.\n"
msgstr "Isang natatanging value ng `modifier_ref`: Inirerekomenda kapag kailangang i-scale ang bawat noise map sa magkakaibang factor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code generates a circuit where the two-qubit gates boxes own an `InjectNoise` annotation with unique `modifier_ref` values.\n"
msgstr "Bumubuo ang sumusunod na code ng circuit kung saan ang mga box ng two-qubit gate ay may hawak na annotation na `InjectNoise` na may mga natatanging value ng `modifier_ref`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select a twirling strategy {#select-a-twirling-strategy}"
msgstr "Pumili ng twirling strategy {#select-a-twirling-strategy}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The boxing pass manager begins by choosing which entangling gates and measurement instructions should appear in the same boxes. Once this is accomplished, boxes will not, in general, be full-width—they will likely include only a subset of the qubits that are active in the circuit or present in the backend target. In typical configurations of the boxing pass manager, since all qubits that a box instruction acts on are twirled (even those for which no instruction inside the box act on), having partial-width boxes affects the noise-tailoring effects of twirling. The idling qubits are not twirled and can, for example, build up coherent errors while the box is applied. The `twirling_strategy` provides options for extending the qubits owned by each box, thereby modifying the number of idling qubits:\n"
msgstr "Nagsisimula ang boxing pass manager sa pagpili kung aling mga entangling gate at measurement instruction ang dapat lumitaw sa parehong mga box. Kapag nagawa na ito, sa pangkalahatan ay hindi full-width ang mga box—malamang na subset lang ng mga qubit na aktibo sa circuit o naroroon sa backend target ang laman ng mga ito. Sa karaniwang configuration ng boxing pass manager, dahil lahat ng qubit na inaaksyunan ng isang box instruction ay ti-nitwirl (kahit ang mga walang instruction sa loob ng box na umaaksyon sa kanila), naaapektuhan ng pagkakaroon ng partial-width na mga box ang mga noise-tailoring na epekto ng twirling. Ang mga idling na qubit ay hindi ti-nitwirl at maaaring, halimbawa, makaipon ng mga coherent error habang ina-apply ang box. Nagbibigay ang `twirling_strategy` ng mga opsyon para palawigin ang mga qubit na hawak ng bawat box, kaya binabago ang bilang ng mga idling na qubit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"active\"` (default) does not extend the boxes to any idling qubits.\n"
msgstr "Ang `\"active\"` (default) ay hindi nagpapalawig ng mga box sa anumang idling na qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"active_accum\"` extends all boxes to those qubits that have already been acted on by a prior instruction in the circuit. This is useful if you want to leave qubits at the start of the circuit in their ground state for as long as possible by not twirling them until they become active.\n"
msgstr "Pinapalawig ng `\"active_accum\"` ang lahat ng box sa mga qubit na naaksyunan na ng naunang instruction sa circuit. Kapaki-pakinabang ito kung gusto mong iwan ang mga qubit sa simula ng circuit sa kanilang ground state hangga't maaari sa pamamagitan ng hindi pag-twirl sa mga ito hanggang maging aktibo ang mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"active_circuit\"` extends all boxes to those qubits that are acted on by any instruction in the circuit. This is useful if you have a structured circuit with repeated entangling layers and you want to minimize the number of unique boxes because each one needs to have its noise learned.\n"
msgstr "Pinapalawig ng `\"active_circuit\"` ang lahat ng box sa mga qubit na inaaksyunan ng anumang instruction sa circuit. Kapaki-pakinabang ito kung mayroon kang structured na circuit na may paulit-ulit na entangling layer at gusto mong bawasan ang bilang ng mga natatanging box dahil kailangang matutunan ang noise ng bawat isa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"all\"` extends all boxes to all qubits in all quantum registers of the circuit. This is useful as an extension to `\"active_circuit\"` where you want all qubits in the QPU to always be twirled.\n"
msgstr "Pinapalawig ng `\"all\"` ang lahat ng box sa lahat ng qubit sa lahat ng quantum register ng circuit. Kapaki-pakinabang ito bilang extension ng `\"active_circuit\"` kung gusto mong laging ma-twirl ang lahat ng qubit sa QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following example, each of the strategies is applied to the base circuit, then the results are drawn.\n"
msgstr "Sa sumusunod na halimbawa, ina-apply ang bawat estratehiya sa base circuit, pagkatapos ay iginuguhit ang mga resulta.\n"

