# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify how to treat barriers {#specify-how-to-treat-barriers}"
msgstr "Tukuyin kung paano tratuhin ang mga barrier {#specify-how-to-treat-barriers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, barriers are removed from the circuit after all entangling gates and measurement instructions have been boxed as instructed, including their extensions due to the `twirling_strategy` selection, but before single-qubit gates are added to the box immediately on their right, if possible.\n"
msgstr "Bilang default, inaalis ang mga barrier sa circuit pagkatapos mai-box ang lahat ng entangling gate at measurement instruction ayon sa tagubilin, kasama ang mga extension ng mga ito dahil sa napiling `twirling_strategy`, pero bago idagdag ang mga single-qubit gate sa box na agad nasa kanan ng mga ito, kung posible.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, the following circuit contains a barrier:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa, ang sumusunod na circuit ay naglalaman ng isang barrier:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/f2343807597155ab5301205803954b95d29ba0d7370440bd861439fd83d1a193.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/f2343807597155ab5301205803954b95d29ba0d7370440bd861439fd83d1a193.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/f2343807597155ab5301205803954b95d29ba0d7370440bd861439fd83d1a193.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/f2343807597155ab5301205803954b95d29ba0d7370440bd861439fd83d1a193.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The default behavior prevents the two entangling gates from ending up in the same box, although it lets the single-qubit gates be absorbed into the next available box despite the barrier.\n"
msgstr "Pinipigilan ng default na gawi na mapunta sa parehong box ang dalawang entangling gate, bagama't hinahayaan nitong masipsip ang mga single-qubit gate sa susunod na available na box sa kabila ng barrier.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/7e0812ac6b3f2405c765338ab25c2e9179165a7257ef1d996bea99f94cb39ca6.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/7e0812ac6b3f2405c765338ab25c2e9179165a7257ef1d996bea99f94cb39ca6.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/7e0812ac6b3f2405c765338ab25c2e9179165a7257ef1d996bea99f94cb39ca6.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/7e0812ac6b3f2405c765338ab25c2e9179165a7257ef1d996bea99f94cb39ca6.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting `remove_barriers` to `'never'` preserves the barriers so that single-qubit gates are constrained.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagtatakda ng `remove_barriers` sa `'never'` ay pinapanatili ang mga barrier kaya nalilimitahan ang mga single-qubit gate.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/6b57e625509dd8ca55fbd96994398b03ac2fe6f76f21535db9bd042d4c68c987.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/6b57e625509dd8ca55fbd96994398b03ac2fe6f76f21535db9bd042d4c68c987.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/6b57e625509dd8ca55fbd96994398b03ac2fe6f76f21535db9bd042d4c68c987.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/6b57e625509dd8ca55fbd96994398b03ac2fe6f76f21535db9bd042d4c68c987.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, if the barriers are removed immediately, the entanglers are no longer constrained to end up in separate boxes.\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, kung agad na aalisin ang mga barrier, hindi na limitado ang mga entangler na mapunta sa magkakahiwalay na box.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/9a44c59a05a44a3e8f0ce9b7edd3ccc2896c6a68fb00ed110a7e225f52a7ca73.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/9a44c59a05a44a3e8f0ce9b7edd3ccc2896c6a68fb00ed110a7e225f52a7ca73.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/9a44c59a05a44a3e8f0ce9b7edd3ccc2896c6a68fb00ed110a7e225f52a7ca73.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/9a44c59a05a44a3e8f0ce9b7edd3ccc2896c6a68fb00ed110a7e225f52a7ca73.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "How stratification works {#how-stratification-works}"
msgstr "Paano gumagana ang stratification {#how-stratification-works}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The boxing pass manager runs two key passes in sequence:\n"
msgstr "Nagpapatakbo ang boxing pass manager ng dalawang pangunahing pass nang sunud-sunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`GroupGatesIntoBoxes`** — Stratifies entangling gates into boxes. Single-qubit gates are ignored at this stage; only two-qubit gates are grouped.\n"
msgstr "**`GroupGatesIntoBoxes`** — Ini-stratify ang mga entangling gate sa mga box. Hindi pinapansin ang mga single-qubit gate sa yugtong ito; mga two-qubit gate lang ang ig-ni-group.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`AbsorbSingleQubitGates`** — Absorbs each single-qubit gate into the nearest eligible box to its right.\n"
msgstr "**`AbsorbSingleQubitGates`** — Sinisipsip ang bawat single-qubit gate sa pinakamalapit na karapat-dapat na box sa kanan nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "During stratification, `GroupGatesIntoBoxes` traverses the circuit DAG in topological order and places each two-qubit gate in the **earliest group** whose qubits are not yet occupied. Three kinds of instructions act as **delimiters** that flush the current group for their qubits, forcing subsequent gates on those qubits into a new group:\n"
msgstr "Sa stratification, tinatahak ng `GroupGatesIntoBoxes` ang circuit DAG sa topological order at inilalagay ang bawat two-qubit gate sa **pinakamaagang group** na ang mga qubit ay hindi pa okupado. Tatlong uri ng instruction ang kumikilos bilang mga **delimiter** na nag-fflush ng kasalukuyang group para sa mga qubit nila, na nagtutulak sa mga susunod na gate sa mga qubit na iyon sa bagong group:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Barriers**\n"
msgstr "**Mga Barrier**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Existing box instructions**\n"
msgstr "**Mga umiiral na box instruction**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Measurements**\n"
msgstr "**Measurements**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Single-qubit gates are not delimiters — they have no effect on grouping and are left for `AbsorbSingleQubitGates` to handle. No commutativity analysis is currently performed; the grouping respects the topological order of the circuit as-is.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga single-qubit gate ay hindi mga delimiter — wala silang epekto sa grouping at iniiwan para hawakan ng `AbsorbSingleQubitGates`. Sa kasalukuyan, walang commutativity analysis na isinasagawa; sinusunod ng grouping ang topological order ng circuit kung ano ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"why-remove-barriers-after-stratification-is-the-recommended-default\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why `remove_barriers=\"after_stratification\"` is the recommended default {#why-remove_barriersafter_stratification-is-the-recommended-default}"
msgstr "Bakit ang `remove_barriers=\"after_stratification\"` ang inirerekomendang default {#why-remove_barriersafter_stratification-is-the-recommended-default}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The default mode is `\"after_stratification\"` because it combines two benefits:\n"
msgstr "Ang default na mode ay `\"after_stratification\"` dahil pinagsasama nito ang dalawang benepisyo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers constrain how entangling gates are grouped (they act as delimiters during stratification).\n"
msgstr "Nililimitahan ng mga barrier kung paano ig-ni-group ang mga entangling gate (kumikilos sila bilang mga delimiter habang stratification).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers are removed *before* [`AbsorbSingleQubitGates`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-passes-absorb-single-qubit-gates#samplomatic.transpiler.passes.AbsorbSingleQubitGates \"samplomatic.transpiler.passes.AbsorbSingleQubitGates\") runs, so single-qubit gates can still flow across former barrier positions and be absorbed into the nearest box.\n"
msgstr "Inaalis ang mga barrier *bago* tumakbo ang [`AbsorbSingleQubitGates`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-passes-absorb-single-qubit-gates#samplomatic.transpiler.passes.AbsorbSingleQubitGates \"samplomatic.transpiler.passes.AbsorbSingleQubitGates\"), kaya ang mga single-qubit gate ay nakakadaan pa rin sa mga dating posisyon ng barrier at nasisipsip sa pinakamalapit na box.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By contrast:\n"
msgstr "Sa kabilang banda:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"never\"` keeps barriers throughout, which traps single-qubit gates between a barrier and a box, preventing their absorption and leaving untwirled rotations in the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Pinapanatili ng `\"never\"` ang mga barrier sa buong proseso, na nagkukulong sa mga single-qubit gate sa pagitan ng barrier at box, kaya napipigilan ang pagsipsip sa mga ito at naiiwan ang mga untwirled na rotation sa circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"immediately\"` removes barriers before stratification, so they have no effect on grouping.\n"
msgstr "Inaalis ng `\"immediately\"` ang mga barrier bago ang stratification, kaya wala silang epekto sa grouping.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"finally\"` is useful when you want barriers in the output circuit (for example, for visualization), but single-qubit gates between a barrier and a box are not absorbed.\n"
msgstr "Kapaki-pakinabang ang `\"finally\"` kapag gusto mo ng mga barrier sa output circuit (halimbawa, para sa visualization), pero hindi nasisipsip ang mga single-qubit gate sa pagitan ng barrier at box.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Box ISA circuits with barriers {#box-isa-circuits-with-barriers}"
msgstr "I-box ang mga ISA circuit gamit ang mga barrier {#box-isa-circuits-with-barriers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuits with a repeated structure — such as Trotterized Hamiltonian simulations, variational ansatze, and error amplification sequences — are typically built programmatically and then transpiled to ISA form. Manually adding boxes to a transpiled circuit is cumbersome, so the natural workflow is as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga circuit na may paulit-ulit na istruktura — gaya ng mga Trotterized Hamiltonian simulation, variational ansatze, at error amplification sequence — ay karaniwang binubuo sa pamamagitan ng code at saka ni-transpile sa ISA form. Nakakapagod ang manu-manong pagdaragdag ng mga box sa isang na-transpile na circuit, kaya ang natural na workflow ay ang sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the logical circuit, inserting **barriers** at the layer boundaries you want to become box boundaries.\n"
msgstr "Buuin ang logical circuit, at maglagay ng mga **barrier** sa mga hangganan ng layer na gusto mong maging hangganan ng box.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile to ISA circuits. Qiskit’s transpiler preserves barriers through routing and optimization.\n"
msgstr "I-transpile sa mga ISA circuit. Pinapanatili ng transpiler ng Qiskit ang mga barrier sa routing at optimization.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\") on the ISA circuit.\n"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\") sa ISA circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers are needed when the end of one layer does not cover all qubits. The greedy algorithm would otherwise place gates from the next layer—on those “free” qubits—into the same group. As a concrete example, consider a two-step Heisenberg ZZ simulation on a 5-qubit ring. Each Trotter step has three bond layers: even bonds `(0,1), (2,3)`, odd bonds `(1,2), (3,4)`, and the wrap bond `(4,0)`. After the odd-bond layer, qubits 0 and 4 are both free. Without a barrier, the wrap bond `(4,0)` gets greedy-grouped with bonds from the *next* Trotter step that use those free qubits, mixing gates from different steps in the same box.\n"
msgstr "Kailangan ang mga barrier kapag hindi sakop ng dulo ng isang layer ang lahat ng qubit. Kung wala ito, ilalagay ng greedy algorithm sa iisang grupo ang mga gate mula sa susunod na layer—sa mga \"libreng\" qubit na iyon. Bilang konkretong halimbawa, isaalang-alang ang dalawang-hakbang na Heisenberg ZZ simulation sa isang 5-qubit na ring. Bawat Trotter step ay may tatlong bond layer: ang even bond `(0,1), (2,3)`, ang odd bond `(1,2), (3,4)`, at ang wrap bond `(4,0)`. Pagkatapos ng odd-bond layer, parehong libre ang qubit 0 at 4. Kung walang barrier, ang wrap bond `(4,0)` ay ma-greedy-group kasama ng mga bond mula sa *susunod* na Trotter step na gumagamit ng mga libreng qubit na iyon, kaya nagkakahalo sa iisang box ang mga gate mula sa magkakaibang step.\n"

