# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect and modify annotations {#inspect-and-modify-annotations}"
msgstr "Suriin at baguhin ang mga annotation {#inspect-and-modify-annotations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After auto-boxing, you might want to inspect the annotations on specific boxes or adjust them. For example, to add noise injection, remove annotations, or change a twirling group. Samplomatic provides a set of utility functions in [`samplomatic.utils`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/utils#module-samplomatic.utils \"samplomatic.utils\") for this purpose. All of them return a **new circuit** without modifying the original.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos ng auto-boxing, maaaring gusto mong suriin ang mga annotation sa mga partikular na box o ayusin ang mga ito. Halimbawa, para magdagdag ng noise injection, magtanggal ng mga annotation, o magpalit ng twirling group. Nagbibigay ang Samplomatic ng isang set ng mga utility function sa [`samplomatic.utils`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/utils#module-samplomatic.utils \"samplomatic.utils\") para sa layuning ito. Lahat ng mga ito ay nagbabalik ng **bagong circuit** nang hindi binabago ang orihinal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`extend_annotations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/utils-extend-annotations#samplomatic.utils.extend_annotations \"samplomatic.utils.extend_annotations\") appends one or more annotations to every box in the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang [`extend_annotations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/utils-extend-annotations#samplomatic.utils.extend_annotations \"samplomatic.utils.extend_annotations\") ay nagdaragdag ng isa o higit pang annotation sa bawat box sa circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`filter_annotations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/utils-filter-annotations#samplomatic.utils.filter_annotations \"samplomatic.utils.filter_annotations\") keeps only annotations of specified types, removing the rest. [`replace_annotations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/utils-replace-annotations#samplomatic.utils.replace_annotations \"samplomatic.utils.replace_annotations\") applies a callable to each annotation; the callable returns a list of annotations to substitute in its place (return `[]` to remove, a single-element list to replace, or a multi-element list to expand).\n"
msgstr "Ang [`filter_annotations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/utils-filter-annotations#samplomatic.utils.filter_annotations \"samplomatic.utils.filter_annotations\") ay nag-iiwan lamang ng mga annotation ng mga tinukoy na uri at inaalis ang iba. Ang [`replace_annotations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/utils-replace-annotations#samplomatic.utils.replace_annotations \"samplomatic.utils.replace_annotations\") ay naglalapat ng isang callable sa bawat annotation; ang callable ay nagbabalik ng listahan ng mga annotation na ipapalit (magbalik ng `[]` para alisin, isang list na may iisang elemento para palitan, o isang list na may maraming elemento para palawakin).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The general-purpose [`map_annotations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/utils-map-annotations#samplomatic.utils.map_annotations \"samplomatic.utils.map_annotations\") function accepts any callable that maps a list of annotations to a new list, giving you full control over per-box transformations. [`strip_annotations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/utils-strip-annotations#samplomatic.utils.strip_annotations \"samplomatic.utils.strip_annotations\") is a convenience wrapper that removes all annotations from every box.\n"
msgstr "Ang pangkalahatang-gamit na function na [`map_annotations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/utils-map-annotations#samplomatic.utils.map_annotations \"samplomatic.utils.map_annotations\") ay tumatanggap ng anumang callable na nagmamapa ng listahan ng mga annotation sa bagong listahan, kaya may buo kang kontrol sa mga transformation kada box. Ang [`strip_annotations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/utils-strip-annotations#samplomatic.utils.strip_annotations \"samplomatic.utils.strip_annotations\") ay isang convenience wrapper na nag-aalis ng lahat ng annotation mula sa bawat box.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For bulk changes like adding [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") to all gate boxes, the `inject_noise_targets` parameter of [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\") is the most concise option. These utilities are useful for selective per-box edits that the pass manager parameters do not cover.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga bulk na pagbabago tulad ng pagdaragdag ng [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") sa lahat ng gate box, ang parameter na `inject_noise_targets` ng [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\") ang pinakamaikling opsyon. Kapaki-pakinabang ang mga utility na ito para sa mga piling pag-edit kada box na hindi sakop ng mga parameter ng pass manager.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a circuit {#build-a-circuit}"
msgstr "Bumuo ng circuit {#build-a-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every pass manager produced by [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\") returns circuits that can be successfully turned into a template/samplex pair by [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\"). For example, the following code calls the [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function on a circuit produced by a boxing pass manager.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat pass manager na nilikha ng [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\") ay nagbabalik ng mga circuit na matagumpay na magagawang template/samplex pair ng [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\"). Halimbawa, tinatawag ng sumusunod na code ang function na [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") sa isang circuit na nilikha ng boxing pass manager.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To ensure that any transpiled circuit can be successfully built, the pass managers know how to include additional boxes when they are needed. For example, consider the circuit below, which ends with an unmeasured qubit `0`.\n"
msgstr "Upang matiyak na matagumpay na mabubuo ang anumang na-transpile na circuit, alam ng mga pass manager kung paano magsama ng karagdagang mga box kapag kailangan ang mga ito. Halimbawa, isaalang-alang ang circuit sa ibaba, na nagtatapos sa isang hindi na-measure na qubit `0`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/0452779799470d2deb4d32ce19f5aa28dfe8055a064e67c0e8e5684389845b0f.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/0452779799470d2deb4d32ce19f5aa28dfe8055a064e67c0e8e5684389845b0f.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/0452779799470d2deb4d32ce19f5aa28dfe8055a064e67c0e8e5684389845b0f.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/0452779799470d2deb4d32ce19f5aa28dfe8055a064e67c0e8e5684389845b0f.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drawing left-dressed boxes around the gates and measurements would result in a circuit that has uncollected virtual gates on qubit `0`, and calling [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") on this circuit would result in an error. To avoid this, the pass managers returned by [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\") can add right-dressed boxes to act as collectors. For example, in the following code, qubit `0` is terminated by a right-dressed box that picks up the uncollected virtual gate. The single-qubit gates acting on qubit `0` are also placed inside the box in order to minimize the depth of the resulting circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagguhit ng mga left-dressed box sa paligid ng mga gate at measurement ay magreresulta sa circuit na may mga hindi nakolektang virtual gate sa qubit `0`, at ang pagtawag sa [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") sa circuit na ito ay magreresulta sa error. Para maiwasan ito, ang mga pass manager na ibinabalik ng [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\") ay maaaring magdagdag ng mga right-dressed box na magsisilbing collector. Halimbawa, sa sumusunod na code, ang qubit `0` ay tinatapos ng isang right-dressed box na kumukuha ng hindi nakolektang virtual gate. Inilalagay rin sa loob ng box ang mga single-qubit gate na kumikilos sa qubit `0` para mabawasan ang depth ng resultang circuit.\n"

